---
import CompanyShell from '../components/CompanyShell.astro';
---

<CompanyShell
  title="Privacy Policy — Camm Studios"
  description="Privacy Policy for Camm Studios apps. Learn how we handle your data."
>
  <div class="shell">
    <header class="page-head">
      <p class="kicker kicker--rule">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="display-lg">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="mono-note">Last updated: March 18, 2026</p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Camm Studios ("we", "our", or "us") operates mobile applications (the "Apps"). This Privacy
        Policy explains how we collect, use, and protect your information when you use our Apps.
        App-specific policies for
        <a href="https://bronzed.cammstudios.com/privacy">Bronzed</a> and
        <a href="https://stellar.cammstudios.com/privacy">Stellar</a> supplement this policy.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>

      <h3>Information You Provide</h3>
      <p>
        Our Apps store your content (such as journal entries, affirmations, vision board images, and
        preferences) <strong>locally on your device</strong>. We do not transmit this content to our
        servers.
      </p>
      <p>
        During onboarding, some of our Apps may ask you for profile information such as your first
        name, age range, gender, and personal interests. This information is used to personalise
        your experience and may be shared with our third-party analytics and paywall services (see
        Section 4 below).
      </p>

      <h3>Automatically Collected Information</h3>
      <p>We collect usage data to improve our Apps through third-party analytics services:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Device information:</strong> Device model, operating system version, and app version</li>
        <li>
          <strong>Usage analytics:</strong> Feature usage events (e.g. screens viewed, actions
          taken), collected via <strong>PostHog</strong>
        </li>
        <li><strong>App lifecycle events:</strong> App launches, sessions, and background transitions</li>
        <li><strong>Crash reports:</strong> Anonymous crash data to help us fix bugs</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        This data is associated with anonymous identifiers and does not include your name, email, or
        locally stored content.
      </p>

      <h3>Subscription Information</h3>
      <p>
        All subscription purchases and billing are processed by Apple through the App Store. We do
        not collect or store your payment information. Subscription status is managed through
        <strong>Superwall</strong> or <strong>RevenueCat</strong> (depending on the app), which
        receive an anonymous user identifier and purchase receipts to verify your subscription.
      </p>

      <h2>2. How We Use Your Information</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To provide and maintain our Apps</li>
        <li>To personalise your experience (e.g. tailored paywall offers)</li>
        <li>To improve app performance and fix bugs through analytics</li>
        <li>To verify subscription status</li>
        <li>To understand how features are used so we can improve them</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. Data Storage and Security</h2>
      <p>
        Your personal content (journal entries, affirmations, vision board items, etc.) is stored
        <strong>only on your device</strong> and is not backed up to our servers. If you delete the
        App, your locally stored data will be permanently deleted.
      </p>
      <p>
        Profile attributes collected during onboarding and usage analytics are transmitted to our
        third-party service providers (see Section 4). We rely on these providers' security
        practices to protect this data.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Third-Party Services</h2>
      <p>Our Apps use the following third-party services that may receive data:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>PostHog</strong> (analytics) — Receives anonymous usage events, device
          information, and user attributes. Data is processed on servers in the United States.
          <a href="https://posthog.com/privacy" rel="noopener">PostHog Privacy Policy</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Superwall</strong> (paywall and subscription management) — Receives anonymous user
          identifiers, user profile attributes, and subscription status for paywall personalisation.
          <a href="https://superwall.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Superwall Privacy Policy</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>RevenueCat</strong> (subscription management) — Receives anonymous user
          identifiers, purchase receipts, and subscription status to unlock premium access and
          restore purchases.
          <a href="https://www.revenuecat.com/privacy" rel="noopener">RevenueCat Privacy Policy</a>
        </li>
        <li><strong>Apple App Store</strong> — Processes all subscription purchases and billing</li>
        <li>
          <strong>TikTok Events SDK</strong> (attribution and advertising analytics) — Receives app
          install and event data (e.g. app opens, purchases), device information (device model, OS
          version), and advertising identifiers (IDFA, if you have granted permission) to measure
          advertising campaign performance. Data is processed by TikTok Inc. and may be transferred
          to servers in the United States and other countries.
          <a href="https://www.tiktok.com/legal/page/global/privacy-policy/en" rel="noopener">TikTok Privacy Policy</a>
        </li>
        <li><strong>Vercel</strong> — Hosts our websites and collects anonymous web analytics</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We do not sell your personal information to any third party.</p>

      <h2>5. Data Retention</h2>
      <p>
        Locally stored data persists on your device until you delete the App. Analytics data held by
        third-party providers is retained according to their respective data retention policies. We
        do not maintain our own servers or databases containing your personal data.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Children's Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        Our Apps are not intended for anyone under the age of 18. We do not knowingly collect
        personal information from children. If you are under 18, please do not use our Apps. If we
        learn that we have collected information from a person under 18, we will take steps to
        delete that information.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Your Rights</h2>

      <h3>All Users</h3>
      <p>
        Since your content is stored locally on your device, you have full control over it at all
        times. You can delete all locally stored data by deleting the App.
      </p>

      <h3>European Economic Area (GDPR)</h3>
      <p>If you are located in the EEA, you have the right to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Access the personal data we hold about you</li>
        <li>Request correction of inaccurate data</li>
        <li>Request deletion of your data</li>
        <li>Object to or restrict processing of your data</li>
        <li>Data portability</li>
        <li>Withdraw consent at any time</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Our legal basis for processing is legitimate interest (improving our Apps) and consent
        (profile data provided during onboarding). To exercise your rights, contact us at the email
        below.
      </p>

      <h3>California Residents (CCPA)</h3>
      <p>If you are a California resident, you have the right to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Know what personal information we collect and how it is used</li>
        <li>Request deletion of your personal information</li>
        <li>Opt out of the sale of your personal information (we do not sell your data)</li>
        <li>Non-discrimination for exercising your privacy rights</li>
      </ul>
      <p>To exercise your rights, contact us at the email below.</p>

      <h3>Australian Users (Privacy Act 1988)</h3>
      <p>
        If you are located in Australia, you have the right to access and correct personal
        information we hold about you under the Australian Privacy Principles. To make a request,
        contact us at the email below.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Changes to This Policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. We will notify you of any material
        changes by updating the "Last updated" date at the top of this page. Your continued use of
        our Apps after changes are posted constitutes acceptance of the updated policy.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Contact Us</h2>
      <p>
        If you have any questions about this Privacy Policy or wish to exercise your privacy rights,
        please contact us:
      </p>
      <p><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:info@cammstudios.com">info@cammstudios.com</a></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</CompanyShell>
